No Microsoft product artwork is distributed inside the Horizon application.
Where the About page shows the Foundry Local icon, that image is read at
runtime from the copy installed on the user's own machine (src/brand.js) and
remains Microsoft's property. If Foundry Local is not installed, Horizon falls
back to its own original glyph and no Microsoft artwork is shown.

The project website under docs/ is a static page with no runtime, so it cannot
read anything from a visitor's machine. Where it shows a third-party mark
beside a download link, that mark is a simplified rendering used to identify
the destination, and is not a claim of affiliation or endorsement.

Models downloaded through Foundry Local carry their own licences, shown
in the model catalogue under Settings.